{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1447608-vampire-hunting-for-the-thrifty-customer","id":1447608,"title":"Vampire Hunting for the thrifty customer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-05T11:42:16-07:00","id":1447608,"title":"Vampire Hunting for the thrifty customer","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> If this has been answered before, I'll happily check an existing thread.<br /> <br /> My group has a Tzimisce hunting them, and the wealthiest of them has Resources 2 at best. But they do have some good skills in crafting and occult. What affordable and effective methods of vampire Hunting do you recommend? I'm currently thinking of stuff like crossbows, or covering a propane tank in stakes and hoping for the best.<br /> <br /> What are some your favourite budget vampire Hunting tools?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25927-lolotovcocktail","name":"LolotovCocktail","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:25:27-07:00","id":1447629,"title":"","content":"I would think Vampire hunting to be rather inexpensive.<br /> <br /> -Molotov cocktails are cheap and effective.<br /> -Butane torches could easily make a vampire think twice about getting in close.<br /> -Wooden spears are a better option then stakes.<br /> -If your hunters are willing to sacrifice a vehicle, running over a vamp and then torching the car is a viable tactic. <br /> -Shotguns are good against anything, although it's true vampires will only take bashing called shots should still be able to disable a vamp and it wouldn't take log for that damage to roll over into lethal.<br /> -gasoline and styrofoam mix together to make a sort of sticky poor man's napalm. (or so I'm told)<br /> -Bear traps might cost a little up front, but should be reusable and could easily take away a vampires speed advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T07:25:34-07:00","id":1447710,"title":"","content":"Idle notice: this is Chronicles, not World. We don't have Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T16:35:49-07:00","id":1454104,"title":"","content":"Even though this question was likely posted to the wrong Hunter venue, I have to chime in with suggestions.<br /> <br /> I have to second the Molotov cocktails. They're too easy to make. The poor man's hand grenade. <br /> <br /> Also, crossbows with hand carved wooden bolts. Cheap pistol grip crossbows cost about $50 IRL. Hunting crossbows can be a couple hundred bucks on the low end. The idea is to try and stake the vamp at range. <br /> <br /> On the subject of shotguns look up the &quot;gimmick ammo&quot; known as Dragon's Breath. It's actually reasonably priced, but you have to get it mail order.<br /> <br /> Also a truck. No really, just a pickup truck. There is an anti-werewolf Tactic in the Spirit Slayers supplement to Hunter where you get one hunter to goad the monster into chasing them, Scooby Doo-style, and another hunter sits in a pickup truck or other car in an ambush spot and waits for their buddy to run past. Then the person in the car hits the gas and runs over the monster chasing their friend. That's how it works in theory. There are dice rolls involved obviously, and a risk of the hunter in the car missing the monster or running over &quot;Shaggy and Scooby&quot; if they don't time flooring the gas just right. But it's otherwise a great all around tactic for hunters of any budget to use against big nasties, provided at least one of them has a car. It's not even necessary to torch the car. Just put it in reverse and run the sucker over again. And again, and again.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T19:58:06-07:00","id":1457069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1447608-vampire-hunting-for-the-thrifty-customer